# Lecture 10B

## Biotechnology: Group Project
## Dr. Neil Voss
## Nov 5, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Choose a company that your group can explain and develop together.
- Plan a connected scientific presentation and a complete business plan.
- Use the current project milestones, required sections, and evaluation criteria.

=== layout: section

# The Group Company Project

=== layout: one-panel

# Individual Projects Are Complete

@body

- Your individual pitch, executive summary, and milestones work now become evidence for a shared company.
- The group project can select one individual proposal and revise its name, product, market, or scientific strategy.
- This is a deeper scientific and business case, not several individual projects stapled together.
- Your group needs one clear company story, shared evidence, and a final product that reads as one document.

