=== layout: section

# Work as One Company

=== layout: one-panel

# Collaboration That Holds Together

@body

- Start the presentation and business plan early in shared documents.
- Agree on the company's terms, evidence, visual style, and strategy before drafting deeply.
- Have at least two people review each major section.
- Use roles when useful: coordinator, researcher, formatter, and editor.
- Every member remains responsible for both the science and the communication.

=== layout: two-panels

# Roles Help; Silos Hurt

@left

## Useful roles

- Coordinator: schedules and checks progress
- Researcher: finds and verifies evidence
- Formatter: makes visuals consistent
- Editor: improves clarity and flow

@right

## Avoid this outcome

- One person writes a section alone.
- Sections use different names or evidence.
- The final document reads like unrelated reports.
- A name appears on the submission without meaningful work.

=== layout: section

# Group Presentation

=== layout: one-panel

# Present One Connected Case

@body

- Establish the problem and why it matters before revealing the product.
- Make the biotechnology the center: components, methods, evidence, and limits.
- Compare direct and indirect competitors.
- Explain market, development milestones, and the path forward.
- Give every member a meaningful speaking role.

=== layout: one-panel

# Presentation Structure

@body

- Open with the problem and the people, patients, or systems affected.
- Use the scientific explanation to show why your solution could work.
- Introduce the product as the response to that problem.
- Show what distinguishes it from alternatives.
- Close with development milestones, the team, and the investment case.

=== layout: one-panel

# Presentation Requirements

@body

- Plan for 20-30 minutes. Every member speaks for at least 3 minutes.
- Introduce members as they take responsibility for a part of the story.
- Use an enthusiastic host or transitions when they make the presentation easier to follow.
- Return to members when it helps the explanation; do not divide the talk into disconnected blocks.
- Use short, purposeful videos under 2 minutes. Narrate them yourself whenever possible.

=== layout: one-panel

# Pre-Recorded Presentations

@body

- A pre-recorded presentation is allowed and must meet all presentation requirements.
- Use your own voice. Do not use an AI-generated voice or substitute a video for your explanation.
- Keep the full presentation within 10% of 20-30 minutes.
- Upload instructions and peer-evaluation procedures will be announced in Blackboard before Dec 10.

=== layout: section

# Business Plan

=== layout: one-panel

# Required Sections and Order

@body

- Cover Page and Table of Contents (one page)
- Executive Summary (one page)
- Business and Technology Background
- Market Opportunity
- Management Team
- Investment Summary
- Appendix

=== layout: one-panel

# Business Plan Requirements

@body

- Submit one complete 12-18 page document, with the required sections in that order.
- Explain the problem, relevant science, biotechnology, market, management team, and investment case with evidence, figures, tables, and citations.
- Address direct and indirect competition. State the company's advantage and market niche.
- Include at least three spaced development milestones. A milestone is a step toward the product, not the product itself.

=== layout: one-panel

# Formatting and Submission

@body

- Fully justify paragraphs. Keep the cover page and table of contents on one page, and the executive summary on one page.
- Keep the final document in a shared location and review the complete assembled version together.
- Check the uploaded document before the deadline: pages, figures, tables, citations, and references must survive conversion.
- Submit the complete business plan by Dec 17. Blackboard provides the current upload and contribution-form instructions.

